WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.250
A road in Hampshire, at the height of the Beast from the East.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:08.570
Cars have stopped in the snow, and their drivers will be there until morning.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.270
Elsewhere, roads are blocked and the power is off.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.450
Then the arguments start.

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.970
Some say nothing could have stopped it.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.410
Others say we should have been readier.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:21.430
Could Britain have been readier?

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:29.050
In this mission, you'll find out what a red weather warning really means, and what gets spread on the roads before a freeze.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:36.650
You'll ask whether it's the Gulf Stream that keeps Britain mild, and whether cold like this is becoming more common, or rarer.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.360
Your mission: decide whether Britain could have been readier.
